{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPZdp17TQ1mADgiw5Gft","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #394 as ready to work (`status: done`). The engineer triage role will write the plan, and the engineer worker will build it. The decision is in `.ard/394/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why it's ready:** The issue asks for a clear code change. When a job slot frees up, the pool should signal the controller. The controller should then wake only the loops that have waiting work, so the slot is reused within seconds instead of sitting idle until the next poll. It doesn't touch any of the protected paths.\n- **Why only engineer:** engineer is the only triage role that exists besides lead. eng-review has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it will review the pull request anyway and doesn't need adding.\n- **Open issues for a maintainer:**\n  - The change spans the pool and controller packages and changes how the controller wakes loops. That would usually go to an architect, but there's no architect role, so the engineer's plan needs to explain how the new per-loop wakes combine with scheduled ticks and SIGUSR1.\n  - The issue asks for a check that a slot is only released after close-out has written its labels. If some path releases it earlier, the plan will need extra skip logic and a test for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":11651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"741cd1a5-ceaa-4d18-b25b-3ead7ddb057f","uuid":"b14ef41b-e69e-4798-93c1-d9768a5f06c0","timestamp":"2026-11-25T11:25:26.577Z","request_id":"req_011ChPZdoqgr2gAu